  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0201 database is designed to manage information about authors, their books, customers, and reviews. The authors table stores details about each author, including their first and last name, biography, birth day, nationality, and website. The books table contains information about each book, such as its title, ISBN, genre, price, published date, and the ID of the author who wrote it. The books table also includes a foreign key referencing the authors table, establishing a relationship between authors and their written works. The customers table holds data about each customer, including their first and last name, email, passcode, address, and phone number. The orders table tracks each customer's purchases, with a unique order ID, customer ID, order date, total amount, and status. The orders table also references the customers table to link each order to its corresponding customer. The reviews table stores customer feedback about books, with a unique review ID, the ID of the book being reviewed, the ID of the customer who wrote the review, a rating, and a comment. The reviews table includes foreign keys referencing both the books and customers tables, establishing relationships between customers, books, and their reviews.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a comprehensive database system for an online bookstore, named `OnlineBookStore`. This system aims to efficiently manage books, authors, customers, orders, and reviews.\n\nObjectives\n- Design and implement a robust database to support core operations of an online bookstore.\n- Enable essential CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for managing data within the bookstore.\n- Support complex query handling to facilitate comprehensive data retrieval and manipulation.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n- End Users: Customers who interact with the website to browse and purchase books, and provide reviews.\n- Administrators: Internal users responsible for managing inventory, processing orders, and maintaining customer records.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n1. Authors Management:\n   - Store author details such as name, biography, birth date, nationality, and website.\n   - Link books to respective authors.\n\n2. Books Management:\n   - Maintain details about each book, including title, ISBN, genre, price, published date, and associated author.\n   - Track book addition dates.\n\n3. Customers Management:\n   - Capture customer information including name, email, password, address, and phone number.\n   - Securely manage customer login credentials.\n\n4. Orders Processing:\n   - Record customer orders with order date, total amount, and status.\n   - Link orders to customers using unique identifiers.\n\n5. Reviews Handling:\n   - Allow customers to submit reviews with a rating and comments.\n   - Associate reviews with specific books and customers.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n- Ensure secure data handling for customer information, particularly sensitive data like emails and passwords.\n- Optimize database performance for handling large datasets and complex queries.\n- Allow seamless scalability to accommodate an expanding inventory and growing customer base.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0201.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0201\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birth_day` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `genre` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `published_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `passcode` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reviews` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
